{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitPoint"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a unit point to represent a location in a view without having to know"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view’s rendered size. The point stores a value in each dimension that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates the fraction of the view’s size in that dimension — measured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the view’s origin — where the point appears. For example, you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"create a unit point that represents the center of any view by using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value "},{"code":"0.5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for each dimension:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["let unitPoint = UnitPoint(x: 0.5, y: 0.5)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To project the unit point into the rendered view’s coordinate space,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiply each component of the unit point with the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component of the view’s size:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["let projectedPoint = CGPoint(","    x: unitPoint.x * size.width,","    y: unitPoint.y * size.height",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can perform this calculation yourself if you happen to know a view’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, or if you want to use the unit point for some custom purpose, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI typically does this for you to carry out operations that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you request, like when you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Transform a shape using a shape modifier. For example, to rotate a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shape\/rotation(_:anchor:)"},{"type":"text","text":", you indicate an anchor point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that you want to rotate the shape around."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Override the alignment of the view in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Grid"},{"type":"text","text":" cell using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/gridCellAnchor(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" view modifier. The grid aligns the projection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a unit point onto the view with the projection of the same unit point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"onto the cell."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a gradient that has a center, or start and stop points, relative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the shape that you are styling. See the gradient methods in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShapeStyle"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can create custom unit points with explicit values, like the example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above, or you can use one of the built-in unit points that SwiftUI provides,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/zero","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/center","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/topTrailing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The built-in values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"correspond to the alignment positions of the similarly named, built-in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Alignment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A unit point with one or more components outside the range ","type":"text"},{"code":"[0, 1]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"projects to a point outside of the view.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"text":"Layout direction","anchor":"Layout-direction","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a person configures their device to use a left-to-right language like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"English, the system places the view’s origin in its top-left corner,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with positive x toward the right and positive y toward the bottom of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view. In a right-to-left environment, the origin moves to the upper-right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corner, and the positive x direction changes to be toward the left. You","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t typically need to do anything to handle this change, because SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies the change to all aspects of the system. For example, see the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discussion about layout direction in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/HorizontalAlignment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s important to test your app for the different locales that you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distribute your app in. For more information about the localization process,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Xcode\/localization"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SQ","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SH","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"UnitPoint"},"abstract":[{"text":"A normalized 2D point in a view’s coordinate space.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/init(x:y:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/x","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/y"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation